framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR024:
  description |
    Separate Compact semantic state from completed utterance history without
    adding a second realization lifecycle.

problem p001:
  |
    Compact deep psyche still receives lastSpeech inside previous semantic
    state, and Compact expression returns generic speech. Completed utterance
    history is therefore not consistently separated from state and current
    expression across both provider boundaries.

premise pr001:
  |
    Equal text is valid as a new occurrence. Correctness does not depend on
    text inequality, similarity, or a declared reason for repetition.

premise pr002:
  |
    ADR-0004 keeps psyche and outward expression separate. ADR-0008 rejects a
    phrase-ban repair. F-BTL-37 and F-BTL-48 make canonical utterance events
    authoritative.

premise pr003:
  |
    Existing battles retain their immutable contract. Legacy lastSpeech and
    conversationHistory remain readable for old-policy compatibility.

premise pr004:
  |
    The existing battle revision compare-and-save operation is the authoritative
    at-most-once turn commit boundary.

evidence e001:
  |
    CharacterDeepPsycheCompactInput.previous currently includes lastSpeech,
    while conversation.recentExchange separately carries completed dialogue.

evidence e002:
  |
    Compact expression separately receives psyche and conversation fields but
    decodes a generic speech property through Record<string, unknown> and then
    acceptCharacterAgentResult writes that text back to state.lastSpeech.

evidence e003:
  |
    No branch that selects a prior accepted provider-result object was observed
    in acceptCharacterAgentResult. Repository tests already verify rejection of
    a stale battle revision after another advance commits.

decision d001 based_on p001, pr001, pr002, e001, e002:
  |
    Compact deep-psyche and expression contracts use separate expressionState
    and utteranceHistory fields. Semantic state omits lastSpeech and
    conversationHistory.

decision d002 based_on d001, pr001, e002:
  |
    Compact expression output uses nextUtterance and a closed result schema.
    Every otherwise valid result is accepted without comparing prior text or
    asking the model to classify repetition.

decision d003 based_on d001, d002, pr004, e003:
  |
    Reuse the existing battle revision boundary for at-most-once commitment.
    Add no opportunity, receipt, provider-operation, utterance-event identifier,
    secondary idempotency ledger, or runtime cross-opportunity reuse detector.

decision d004 based_on d001, d002, d003, pr003:
  |
    New Compact-policy battles stop using lastSpeech as semantic input or new
    state output. Existing battles and non-Compact processing keep their bound
    compatibility behavior. No new lifecycle identifier is introduced.

decision d005 based_on d001, d002, d004:
  |
    Changed Compact boundaries use closed schemas. any, Record<string, any>,
    Record<string, unknown>, arbitrary record outputs, and z.unknown as a final
    contract are prohibited.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-08, after ADR-0024 and its content-independent repetition
    handling were explained, the product owner instructed, "では、一旦これで
    固めましょう。" The accepted pre-acceptance .think snapshot had SHA-256
    bc9232d5fedb951e3f86420d06a2b32f1c6cb48b4d591c56b5ff2ea7910f1a9e.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on d001, d002, d003, d004, d005, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    ADR-0024 is Accepted at this owner-approved revision. This fixes the
    architectural direction in d001 through d005. It does not itself instruct
    implementation, provider replay, Stage, production, release, or migration;
    those remain separate actions under their own authority boundaries.
